ion key with a new key.'=>'Could not replace the existing encryption key with a new key.','The previous encryption key was defined multiple times in wp-config.php. Instead, manually update your site encryption key.'=>'The previous encryption key was defined multiple times in wp-config.php. Instead, manually update your site encryption key.','Cannot find existing encryption secret in wp-config.php. Instead, manually update your site encryption key.'=>'Cannot find existing encryption secret in wp-config.php. Instead, manually update your site encryption key.','Encountered an empty wp-config.php file.'=>'Encountered an empty wp-config.php file.','Added new encryption key to the wp-config.php file.'=>'Added new encryption key to the wp-config.php file.','Kadence Security does not have permission to write to your wp-config.php file.'=>'Kadence Security does not have permission to write to your wp-config.php file.','The following PHP extension is required: %l.'=>'The following PHP extension is required: %l.' . "\0" . 'The following PHP extensions are required: %l.','The %s PHP extension is required.'=>'The %s PHP extension is required.','You must be running PHP version %s or later.'=>'You must be running PHP version %s or later.','Multisite is not supported.'=>'Multisite is not supported.','Multisite must be enabled.'=>'Multisite must be enabled.','Get More Security'=>'Get More Security','Kadence Security REST API index returned no data.'=>'Kadence Security REST API index returned no data.','Kadence Security REST API index returned a non-200 status code (%d).'=>'Kadence Security REST API index returned a non-200 status code (%d).','REST API index returned no data.'=>'REST API index returned no data.','REST API index returned a non-200 status code (%d).'=>'REST API index returned a non-200 status code (%d).','Cannot connect to index: %l.'=>'Cannot connect to index: %l.','Could not find a REST API URL in the Link header.'=>'Could not find a REST API URL in the Link header.','No Link header was found.'=>'No Link header was found.','Cannot connect to site: %l.'=>'Cannot connect to site: %l.','Could not import \'%1$s\' User Group: %2$s'=>'Could not import \'%1$s\' User Group: %2$s','List of created User Groups'=>'List of created User Groups','Log in now to update.'=>'Log in now to update.','If a security fix is available, update the vulnerable plugin or theme as soon as possible from Your WordPress admin dashboard > Updates page.'=>'If a security fix is available, update the vulnerable plugin or theme as soon as possible from Your WordPress admin dashboard > Updates page.','In the Known Vulnerabilities section of the report, click “Show Details.” If a security fix is available, the report will indicate the latest version number.'=>'In the Known Vulnerabilities section of the report, click “Show Details.” If a security fix is available, the report will indicate the latest version number.','%1$sView the Site Scan Report%2$s available now from your WordPress admin dashboard.'=>'%1$sView the Site Scan Report%2$s available now from your WordPress admin dashboard.','How to View the Report & See Available Updates'=>'How to View the Report & See Available Updates','Vulnerable WordPress plugins and themes are the #1 reason WordPress sites get hacked.'=>'Vulnerable WordPress plugins and themes are the #1 reason WordPress sites get hacked.','What Actions Should I Take?'=>'What Actions Should I Take?','The %1$sSite Scan Scheduling%2$s module sends an email if it discovers an issue or has repeated difficulty conducting the scan.'=>'The %1$sSite Scan Scheduling%2$s module sends an email if it discovers an issue or has repeated difficulty conducting the scan.','Site Scan Results'=>'Site Scan Results','Could not create "%1$s" dashboard for "%2$s": %3$s'=>'Could not create "%1$s" dashboard for "%2$s": %3$s','Security dashboards and cards.'=>'Security dashboards and cards.','Could not ban "%1$s": %2$s'=>'Could not ban "%1$s": %2$s','List of banned IPs.'=>'List of banned IPs.','List of active modules.'=>'List of active modules.','List of settings to display when importing.'=>'List of settings to display when importing.','Hardens your website if you are running outdated software, including checks for old WordPress sites that could be used to compromise your server.'=>'Hardens your website if you are running outdated software, including checks for old WordPress sites that could be used to compromise your server.','Automatically updates vulnerable plugins, themes, and WordPress core for you if it fixes a vulnerability that was found by the Site Scanner.'=>'Automatically updates vulnerable plugins, themes, and WordPress core for you if it fixes a vulnerability that was found by the Site Scanner.','Free your team from mundane updates by removing the need to manually log in to update plugins and themes.'=>'Free your team from mundane updates by removing the need to manually log in to update plugins and themes.','Save time when time is of the utmost importance to patch vulnerabilities before hackers and bots can find and exploit them.'=>'Save time when time is of the utmost importance to patch vulnerabilities before hackers and bots can find and exploit them.','Get all of this in the %1$sSite Scanner Pro%2$s:'=>'Get all of this in the %1$sSite Scanner Pro%2$s:','Get your site patched by Kadence Security Pro before hackers discover vulnerabilities on your site, all without doing a thing.'=>'Get your site patched by Kadence Security Pro before hackers discover vulnerabilities on your site, all without doing a thing.','Kadence Security Pro will <b>automatically update vulnerable plugins and themes for you</b> if a patch is available <b>so you don’t have to manually log in to update</b>.'=>'Kadence Security Pro will <b>automatically update vulnerable plugins and themes for you</b> if a patch is available <b>so you don’t have to manually log in to update</b>.','Go Pro Now to Get Automatic Vulnerability Patching'=>'Go Pro Now to Get Automatic Vulnerability Patching','Pro customers have the best support team available as their security team. Contact the %1$s Kadence Help Desk%2$s for help when you need answers.'=>'Pro customers have the best support team available as their security team. Contact the %1$s Kadence Help Desk%2$s for help when you need answers.','WordPress Security News'=>'WordPress Security News','More Website Security Resources'=>'More Website Security Resources','Import'=>'Import','The \'%s\' feature flag must be enabled.'=>'The \'%s\' feature flag must be enabled.','Excluded Tables'=>'Excluded Tables','Enable XML-RPC'=>'Enable XML-RPC','API Access'=>'API Access','Disables a user’s author page if their post count is 0. This makes it harder for bots to determine usernames by disabling post archives for users that don’t write content for your site.'=>'Disables a user’s author page if their post count is 0. This makes it harder for bots to determine usernames by disabling post archives for users that don’t write content for your site.','Users can only log in using their user’s username. This disables logging in using an email address.'=>'Users can only log in using their user’s username. This disables logging in using an email address.','Users can only log in using their user’s email address. This disables logging in using a username.'=>'Users can only log in using their user’s email address. This disables logging in using a username.','Allow users to log in using their user’s email address or username. This is the default WordPress behavior.'=>'Allow users to log in using their user’s email address or username. This is the default WordPress behaviour.','Email Address and Username'=>'Email Address and Username','Restricted Access'=>'Restricted Access','The WordPress REST API is part of WordPress and provides developers with new ways to manage WordPress. By default, it could give public access to information that you believe is private on your site.'=>'The WordPress REST API is part of WordPress and provides developers with new ways to manage WordPress. By default, it could give public access to information that you believe is private on your site.','By default, the WordPress XML-RPC API allows hundreds of username and password guesses per request. Turn off this setting to prevent attackers from exploiting this feature.'=>'By default, the WordPress XML-RPC API allows hundreds of username and password guesses per request. Turn off this setting to prevent attackers from exploiting this feature.','XML-RPC is fully enabled and will function as normal. Use this setting only if the site must have unrestricted use of XML-RPC.'=>'XML-RPC is fully enabled and will function as normal. Use this setting only if the site must have unrestricted use of XML-RPC.','Only disable pingbacks. Other XML-RPC features will work as normal. Select this setting if you require features such as Jetpack or the WordPress Mobile app.'=>'Only disable pingbacks. Other XML-RPC features will work as normal. Select this setting if you require features such as Jetpack or the WordPress Mobile app.','The WordPress XML-RPC API allows external services to access and modify content on the site. Common example of services that make use of XML-RPC are [the Jetpack plugin](https://jetpack.com), [the WordPress mobile apps](https://wordpress.org/mobile/), and [pingbacks](https://wpbeg.in/IiI0sh). If the site does not use a service that requires XML-RPC, select the “Disable XML-RPC” setting as disabling XML-RPC prevents attackers from using the feature to attack the site.'=>'The WordPress XML-RPC API allows external services to access and modify content on the site. Common example of services that make use of XML-RPC are [the Jetpack plugin](https://jetpack.com), [the WordPress mobile apps](https://wordpress.org/mobile/), and [pingbacks](https://wpbeg.in/IiI0sh). If the site does not use a service that requires XML-RPC, select the “Disable XML-RPC” setting as disabling XML-RPC prevents attackers from using the feature to attack the site.','Disables the WordPress file editor for plugins and themes. Once activated you will need to manually edit files using FTP or other tools.'=>'Disables the WordPress file editor for plugins and themes. Once activated you will need to manually edit files using FTP or other tools.','Increase the security of your website by removing the ability to edit files from the WordPress dashboard and limiting how APIs and users access your site.'=>'Increase the security of your website by removing the ability to edit files from the WordPress dashboard and limiting how APIs and users access your site.','Make changes to the default behavior of WordPress.'=>'Make changes to the default behaviour of WordPress.','User Groups allow you to view and manage the security settings that affect how people interact with your site. Enabling security features per group gives you the flexibility to apply the right level of security to the right people. If a user belongs to multiple groups, all settings enabled in those groups will be applied to that user.'=>'User Groups allow you to view and manage the security settings that affect how people interact with your site. Enabling security features per group gives you the flexibility to apply the right level of security to the right people. If a user belongs to multiple groups, all settings enabled in those groups will be applied to that user.','Use Application Passwords to allow authentication without providing your actual password when using non-traditional login methods such as XML-RPC or the REST API. Application passwords are easily revoked and can never be used in the traditional login process.'=>'Use Application Passwords to allow authentication without providing your actual password when using non-traditional login methods such as XML-RPC or the REST API. Application passwords are easily revoked and can never be used in the traditional login process.','Application Passwords'=>'Application Passwords','By default, when a user logs in via the WordPress Login Page, Kadence Security will prompt them to setup Two-Factor. Optionally, you can skip the two-factor authentication on-boarding process for certain users. Users can still manually enroll in two-factor through their WordPress admin profile.'=>'By default, when a user logs in via the WordPress Login Page, Kadence Security will prompt them to setup Two-Factor. Optionally, you can skip the two-factor authentication on-boarding process for certain users. Users can still manually enroll in two-factor through their WordPress admin profile.','Skip Two-Factor Onboarding'=>'Skip Two-Factor Onboarding','Setup Flow'=>'Setup Flow','Methods'=>'Methods','Customize the text shown to users at the beginning of the Two-Factor onboarding flow.'=>'Customise the text shown to users at the beginning of the Two-Factor onboarding flow.','Onboarding Welcome Text'=>'Onboarding Welcome Text','This simplifies the signup flow for users who require two-factor to be enabled for their account.'=>'This simplifies the signup flow for users who require two-factor to be enabled for their account.','Disable on First Login'=>'Disable on First Login','Select Available Methods'=>'Select Available Methods','Select Methods Manually'=>'Select Methods Manually','All Except Email'=>'All Except Email','All Methods (recommended)'=>'All Methods (recommended)','Kadence Security supports multiple two-factor authentication methods: mobile apps, email messages, and backup codes. Selecting “All Methods” is highly recommended so that users can choose the method that works the best for them.'=>'Kadence Security supports multiple two-factor authentication methods: mobile apps, email messages, and backup codes. Selecting “All Methods” is highly recommended so that users can choose the method that works the best for them.','Authentication Methods Available to Users'=>'Authentication Methods Available to Users','mfa'=>'mfa','multi-factor'=>'multi-factor','2fa'=>'2fa','Two-Factor authentication is a tried and true security method that will stop most automated bot attacks on the WordPress login screen. Once Two-Factor Authentication is enabled here, users can visit their profile settings to enable it on their account.'=>'Two-Factor authentication is a tried and true security method that will stop most automated bot attacks on the WordPress login screen. Once Two-Factor Authentication is enabled here, users can visit their profile settings to enable it on their account.','PHP Execution'=>'PHP Execution','File Access'=>'File Access','Increase security by restricting file access and PHP execution on your server. This can help mitigate arbitrary file upload vulnerabilities from gaining complete control of your server.'=>'Increase security by restricting file access and PHP execution on your server. This can help mitigate arbitrary file upload vulnerabilities from gaining complete control of your server.','Make changes to the server configuration for this site.'=>'Make changes to the server configuration for this site.','Enforces that all connections to the website are made over SSL/TLS.'=>'Enforces that all connections to the website are made over SSL/TLS.','Enforce SSL'=>'Enforce SSL','Detects the correct way to identify user IP addresses based on your server configuration.'=>'Detects the correct way to identify user IP addresses based on your server configuration.','Detects the correct way to identify user IP addresses based on your server configuration by making an API request to Kadence servers. No user information is sent to Kadence. [Read our Privacy Policy](https://go.solidwp.com/solid-privacy-policy).'=>'Detects the correct way to identify user IP addresses based on your server configuration by making an API request to Kadence servers. No user information is sent to Kadence. [Read our Privacy Policy](https://go.solidwp.com/solid-privacy-policy).','This shouldn’t be done periodically, but only if you suspect your site may have been compromised. This will force all users to login again.'=>'This shouldn’t be done periodically, but only if you suspect your site may have been compromised. This will force all users to login again.','Changes the WordPress salts used to secure cookies and security tokens.'=>'Changes the WordPress salts used to secure cookies and security tokens.','Brute force attacks rely on people reusing weak passwords. Password Requirements allow you to force selected users to create a strong password that hasn’t already been compromised.'=>'Brute force attacks rely on people reusing weak passwords. Password Requirements allow you to force selected users to create a strong password that hasn’t already been compromised.','Requiring strong and refusing compromised passwords is the first step in securing your login page.'=>'Requiring strong and refusing compromised passwords is the first step in securing your login page.','Using the Notification Center, you can set the default recipients, enable the security digest email, customize email notifications, and more.'=>'Using the Notification Centre, you can set the default recipients, enable the security digest email, customise email notifications, and more.','API Configuration'=>'API Configuration','Get the weekly WordPress Vulnerability Report and more WordPress security updates sent to your inbox.'=>'Get the weekly WordPress Vulnerability Report and more WordPress security updates sent to your inbox.','Redirection'=>'Redirection','URLs'=>'URLs','The Hide Backend feature isn’t fool proof, and your new login URL could still be exposed by WordPress Core, Plugins, or Themes when printing links to the login page. For example Privacy Request Confirmations or front-end login forms. We recommend using more robust security features like Two-Factor Authentication to secure your WordPress login page.'=>'The Hide Backend feature isn’t fool proof, and your new login URL could still be exposed by WordPress Core, Plugins, or Themes when printing links to the login page. For example Privacy Request Confirmations or front-end login forms. We recommend using more robust security features like Two-Factor Authentication to secure your WordPress login page.','Change the login URL of your site.'=>'Change the login URL of your site.','Refuse Compromised Passwords'=>'Refuse Compromised Passwords','The correct list of server IPs is important to prevent erroneous lockouts and trusted device errors.'=>'The correct list of server IPs is important to prevent erroneous lockouts and trusted device errors.','Determines the list of IP addresses your server uses when making HTTP requests.'=>'Determines the list of IP addresses your server uses when making HTTP requests.','Identify Server IPs'=>'Identify Server IPs','Allow users to manage Kadence Security.'=>'Allow users to manage Kadence Security.','IP Detection'=>'IP Detection','Logging'=>'Logging','Lockout Messages'=>'Lockout Messages','Remove the Security Messages Menu from the Admin Bar. Notifications will only appear on the Kadence Security dashboard and settings pages.'=>'Remove the Security Messages Menu from the Admin Bar. Notifications will only appear on the Kadence Security dashboard and settings pages.','whitelist'=>'whitelist','Automatically Temporarily Authorize IPs'=>'Automatically Temporarily Authorise IPs','The number of lockouts Kadence Security must remember before permanently banning the attacker.'=>'The number of lockouts Kadence Security must remember before permanently banning the attacker.','How many days should Kadence Security remember a lockout? This does not affect the logs generated when creating a lockout.'=>'How many days should Kadence Security remember a lockout? This does not affect the logs generated when creating a lockout.','Days to Remember Lockouts'=>'Days to Remember Lockouts','Minutes to Lockout'=>'Minutes to Lockout','View or flush the generated wp-config.php rules.'=>'View or flush the generated wp-config.php rules.','The “Write to Files” setting must be enabled to automatically flush rules.'=>'The “Write to Files” setting must be enabled to automatically flush rules.','View or flush the generated Server Config rules.'=>'View or flush the generated Server Config rules.','File Writing'=>'File Writing','Check File Permissions'=>'Check File Permissions','Online Files'=>'Online Files','When any WordPress core file or file in a Kadence plugin has been changed on your system, this feature will compare it with the version on WordPress.org or Kadence (as appropriate) to determine if the change was malicious. Currently this feature only works with WordPress core files, plugins on the WordPress.org directory and Kadence plugins (plugins and themes from other sources will be added as available).'=>'When any WordPress core file or file in a Kadence plugin has been changed on your system, this feature will compare it with the version on WordPress.org or Kadence (as appropriate) to determine if the change was malicious. Currently this feature only works with WordPress core files, plugins on the WordPress.org directory and Kadence plugins (plugins and themes from other sources will be added as available).','Compare Files Online'=>'Compare Files Online','Enter a list of file paths to exclude from each File Change scan.'=>'Enter a list of file paths to exclude from each File Change scan.','Excluded Files and Folders'=>'Excluded Files and Folders','Even the best security practices can fail. The key to quickly spotting a security breach is monitoring file changes on your website.<br>While the type of damage malware causes on your website varies greatly, what it does can be boiled down to adding, removing, or modifying files.<br>File Change Detection scans your website’s files and alerts you when changes occur on your website.'=>'Even the best security practices can fail. The key to quickly spotting a security breach is monitoring file changes on your website.<br>While the type of damage malware causes on your website varies greatly, what it does can be boiled down to adding, removing, or modifying files.<br>File Change Detection scans your website’s files and alerts you when changes occur on your website.','Select which experimental features you’d like to enable.'=>'Select which experimental features you’d like to enable.','Enabled Features'=>'Enabled Features','Email Confirmation'=>'Email Confirmation','Allow users to create new Kadence Security Dashboards.'=>'Allow users to create new Kadence Security Dashboards.','Enable Dashboard Creation'=>'Enable Dashboard Creation','See a real-time overview of the security activity on your website with this dynamic dashboard.'=>'See a real-time overview of the security activity on your website with this dynamic dashboard.','Local Brute Force'=>'Local Brute Force','Custom Bans'=>'Custom Bans','Enter a list of user agents that will not be allowed access to your site. Add one user agent per-line.'=>'Enter a list of user agents that will not be allowed access to your site. Add one user agent per-line.','Limiting the number of IPs blocked by the Server Configuration Files (.htaccess and nginx.conf) will help reduce the risk of a server timeout when updating the configuration file. If the number of IPs in the banned list exceeds the Server Configuration File limit, the additional IPs will be blocked using PHP. Blocking IPs at the server level is more efficient than blocking IPs at the application level using PHP.'=>'Limiting the number of IPs blocked by the Server Configuration Files (.htaccess and nginx.conf) will help reduce the risk of a server timeout when updating the configuration file. If the number of IPs in the banned list exceeds the Server Configuration File limit, the additional IPs will be blocked using PHP. Blocking IPs at the server level is more efficient than blocking IPs at the application level using PHP.','Kadence Security automatically adds an IP to the ban list once it meets the Ban Threshold requirements. The Ban Threshold setting can be adjusted in the [Global Settings](itsec://settings/configure/global). You can manually add IPs to the ban list from the Security Dashboard using the Banned IPs card.'=>'Kadence Security automatically adds an IP to the ban list once it meets the Ban Threshold requirements. The Ban Threshold setting can be adjusted in the [Global Settings](itsec://settings/configure/global). You can manually add IPs to the ban list from the Security Dashboard using the Banned IPs card.','List of tables to include in each backup.'=>'List of tables to include in each backup.','List of tables to exclude from each backup.'=>'List of tables to exclude from each backup.','Configuration'=>'Configuration','Scheduling'=>'Scheduling','Specify which tables should be included or excluded from backups. WordPress Core tables are always included.'=>'Specify which tables should be included or excluded from backups. WordPress Core tables are always included.','Backup Tables'=>'Backup Tables','By default, Kadence Security will zip backup files to reduce file size. You may need to turn this off if you are having problems with backups.'=>'By default, Kadence Security will zip backup files to reduce file size. You may need to turn this off if you are having problems with backups.','The path on your machine where backup files should be stored. For added security, it is recommended you do not include it in your website root folder.'=>'The path on your machine where backup files should be stored. For added security, it is recommended you do not include it in your website root folder.','Database backups can help you restore your database in the case of data corruption. However, it is not a complete backup and will not include your site files.'=>'Database backups can help you restore your database in the case of data corruption. However, it is not a complete backup and will not include your site files.','Manually create a database backup or schedule automatic database backups.'=>'