ay important information on your site and serve no purpose to the public once WordPress has been successfully installed.'=>'Prevent public access to readme.html, readme.txt, wp-config.php, install.php, wp-includes, and .htaccess. These files can give away important information on your site and serve no purpose to the public once WordPress has been successfully installed.','Protect System Files'=>'Protect System Files','Prevents users from seeing a list of files in a directory when no index file is present.'=>'Prevents users from seeing a list of files in a directory when no index file is present.','Disable Directory Browsing'=>'Disable Directory Browsing','WordPress Tweaks'=>'WordPress Tweaks','System Tweaks'=>'System Tweaks','Strong Passwords'=>'Strong Passwords','Forces all dashboard access to be served only over an SSL connection.'=>'Forces all dashboard access to be served only over an SSL connection.','Enables secure SSL connection for the front-end (public parts of your site). Turning this off will disable front-end SSL control, turning this on "Per Content" will place a checkbox on the edit page for all posts and pages (near the publish settings) allowing you to turn on SSL for selected pages or posts. Selecting "Whole Site" will force the whole site to use SSL.'=>'Enables secure SSL connection for the front-end (public parts of your site). Turning this off will disable front-end SSL control, turning this on "Per Content" will place a checkbox on the edit page for all posts and pages (near the publish settings) allowing you to turn on SSL for selected pages or posts. Selecting "Whole Site" will force the whole site to use SSL.','SSL for Dashboard'=>'SSL for Dashboard','Front End SSL Mode'=>'Front End SSL Mode','Change WordPress Salts'=>'Change WordPress Salts','WordPress Salts'=>'WordPress Salts','Show Details'=>'Show Details','Malware'=>'Malware','blacklist'=>'blacklist','Error Message: %s'=>'Error Message: %s','The scan failed to properly scan the site.'=>'